    {
      "id": "note_framing",
      "type": "note",
      "position": [
        -560,
        0
      ],
      "params": {
        "text": "ROBUST Designer: closed-loop mRNA optimisation + direct-RNA multi-omics.\n\nROBUST/ACRTC framing: ROBUST-style design loops treat the reward as an ENSEMBLE of cheap, reproducible evaluators rather than one oracle. ACRTC (Adaptive Candidate Refinement with Transparent Controls) is the operating pattern used here: candidates are refined by a group-relative update, every round is checkpointed, and every reward component stays inspectable on disk.\n\nReward-ensemble table (Arm A, per candidate batch):\n  scores_1  multi_objective_scorer prior table (inline JSON; see note_grpo)  maximize\n  telemetry immune_motif_scanner batch burden (per-round context)            minimize (reported)\n  telemetry codon_metrics CAI/GC/Nc of the batch (per-round context)         reported\n  structure rnafold_mfe per-record MFE on the candidate FASTA (ViennaRNA)     iteration artifact\n\nGRPO citations: arXiv 2402.03300 (DeepSeekMath GRPO); arXiv 2605.01513 (MO-GRPO mRNA codon-policy antecedent). The group_relative_optimizer node implements the group z-score advantage A_i=(r_i-mean)/std, advantage-weighted codon counts, softmax temperature, epsilon probability floor and ref_strength mixing toward the reference table (the KL-to-reference analogue).\n\nArm B data: direct-RNA RNA004 POD5 (13 MB example) and its transcriptome reference from the BioinfoSZU/Coral repo, pinned at commit c9be6ecd09117a2555c41fd4eb2af97981500bfa. Dorado RNA004 model rna004_130bps_hac@v5.1.0 from the ONT CDN."
      },
      "ui": {
        "title": "ROBUST/ACRTC Framing",
        "color": "#f59e0b"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note_grpo",
      "type": "note",
      "position": [
        -560,
        640
      ],
      "params": {
        "text": "How the design loop is wired (and its honest limits).\n\nMechanics: while_loop 'design_loop' runs exactly max_iterations=5 rounds. The condition (file_not_exists) is deliberately never re-checked (check_frequency=100 >= max_iterations), so the loop is iteration-count driven; set check_frequency=1 with a sentinel-file condition for convergence-style stopping.\n\nCross-iteration state: the platform's while-loop body re-runs a FLAT node list and only the loop's single 'value' slot crosses iterations. The codon policy and the running-best therefore ride the counter_accumulator loop-state channel (keys: codon_policy, best_candidate, design_round), exactly as the flow-control family prescribes.\n\nGRPO analogy: loop_round -> policy_sampler (pi) samples N=24 synonymous variants -> evaluators -> multi_objective_scorer z-normalises rewards across the GROUP -> group_relative_optimizer computes group advantages and updates the categorical codon policy (softmax + epsilon floor + ref mixing) -> best_so_far tracks the argmax across rounds.\n\nHONEST LIMITS (read before production use): (1) the in-loop evaluators codon_metrics / immune_motif_scanner are single-sequence contracts, so inside the loop they read the whole candidate FASTA as one concatenated batch and act as per-round telemetry, not per-candidate rewards; (2) the per-candidate reward table feeding multi_objective_scorer.scores_1 is therefore a FIXED demo prior over the stable candidate ids (cand_0000..cand_0023) - swap it for live per-candidate evaluator tables when per-candidate reward producers are available; (3) rnafold_mfe in the loop is an iteration artifact (its per-record energies.json lands under runs/<run>/design_loop/iterations/); with the demo prior the composite is constant by construction and the observable learning signal is the policy sharpening (entropy decline in policy_table.json per iteration) and the batch telemetry drift. (4) Platform loops are single-level: no foreach/try_catch INSIDE the while body, which is why the structure evaluators live in the post-loop ensemble under try_catch."
      },
      "ui": {
        "title": "GRPO Loop Notes",
        "color": "#f59e0b"
      }
    },
