      "params": {
        "text": "Arm B: direct-RNA multi-omics ( cleanly separable - delete this group and Arm A still runs).\n\nData: direct-RNA RNA004 example POD5 (13.1 MB) + matching transcriptome reference from BioinfoSZU/Coral, pinned at commit c9be6ecd09117a2555c41fd4eb2af97981500bfa. Dorado simplex model rna004_130bps_hac@v5.1.0 (15.7 MB) from the ONT CDN.\n\nREQUIRES GPU: dorado_basecaller needs a CUDA device and STAGED local model directories (per the dorado node contract, model names/auto-download are intentionally not accepted). The input_directory nodes stage the model zips/POD5 exactly like the ONT long-read template. Note: without an m6A-aware modified-base model staged, MM/ML tags are sparse and the modkit pileup is a plumbing demo; stage an m6A model directory for real m6A calls.\n\nAlignment: minimap2_align uses the 'splice' preset (direct-RNA aware). The canonical direct-RNA refinements -uf -k14 are not exposed by this node's parameter surface (preset + threads only); note them for the wrapped minimap2 path if needed.\n\nLABEL HONESTY: there is no public per-transcript half-life ground truth matched to this demo transcriptome. The half_life_hours column is a SYNTHETIC, deterministic function of the per-transcript features (2.0 + 3.0*mean_mod_fraction + 0.1*mean_coverage) added by the Galaxy Compute-on-rows tool; simple_predictor_train therefore demonstrates the plumbing (features -> join -> train -> metrics), NOT biology. Keep it reproducible or replace the column with real labels."
      },
      "ui": {
        "title": "Arm B: Direct-RNA Notes (GPU)",
        "color": "#8b5cf6"
